# All environments require real individual staff authentication.
# Permanent cloud target: Padova Travel - US Private Trial
# Project ref: unugynfzmxjxifgofxjr | Region: us-east-1
# Copy this file to ignored .env.local. Local mode uses .data/development.
PADOVA_DATABASE_MODE=local
# To activate cloud access, use PADOVA_DATABASE_MODE=supabase and the US
# project's private Connect-panel URL with sslmode=verify-full.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:PRIVATE_PASSWORD@db.unugynfzmxjxifgofxjr.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=verify-full
# For IPv4, use its actual Session pooler URL; user must end .unugynfzmxjxifgofxjr.
# Use port 5432. Add sslrootcert=<URL-encoded-public-CA-file-path> when required.
# Download the project's public CA from Supabase Database Settings > SSL Configuration.
# Keep verify-full enabled; do not disable certificate or hostname validation.
# PADOVA_DB_CA_FILE=absolute-path-to-project-public-CA-certificate.crt
# Missing sslmode defaults to verify-full in memory; explicit weaker modes are rejected.
# Never use the EU Test project, a third project, or a browser service-role key.
# Cloud storage uses existing padova; padova_staging is preserved, never auto-imported.
# The pool assumes padova_app_server; its reviewed extensions must already be installed.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://unugynfzmxjxifgofxjr.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=project-publishable-key
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_SERVER_ONLY_SUPABASE_ADMIN_KEY
# PADOVA_AUTH_ENCRYPTION_KEY=separately-stored-base64-32-byte-random-key
# Keep all three Auth settings server-only; never use NEXT_PUBLIC_ for the admin/key material.
# Sessions use random opaque tokens stored as hashes; no embedded signing secret.
# BACKUP_DIR=owner-controlled-restricted-destination
# BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=separately-stored-base64-32-byte-key
# Complete hosted recovery uses a separate approved read-only backup login.
# PADOVA_BACKUP_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://padova_backup.unugynfzmxjxifgofxjr:PRIVATE_BACKUP_PASSWORD@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=verify-full
# PADOVA_PG_BIN=absolute-path-to-postgresql-17-or-newer-bin
# PADOVA_EVIDENCE_ROOT=absolute-path-to-registered-evidence-files
# Keep backup keys and recovery credentials in the separate Padova Recovery Kit,
# never beside encrypted Google Drive archives. See docs/RECOVERY_RUNBOOK.md.

# Prepared Partnerships extension: configure only for its approved environment.
# PADOVA_PARTNERSHIP_ORIGIN=https://approved-application.example
# PADOVA_PARTNERSHIP_REDIRECT_URIS=https://chatgpt.com/connector_platform_oauth_redirect
# PADOVA_PARTNERSHIP_DOCUMENT_KEY=separately-stored-base64-32-byte-random-key
# Import tooling uses an individual application session, never a database/admin key.
# PADOVA_IMPORT_SESSION_FILE=absolute-private-path-to-individual-session-token.txt
# PADOVA_APPROVED_IMPORT_ORIGIN=https://exact-owner-approved-cutover-origin.example

# Booking email intake (Phase 3) — only Shmuel@ and mindy@padovatravel.com.
# Without OAuth, staff can still forward/paste via POST /api/booking-intake/email.
# Setup: docs/EMAIL_INTAKE_OAUTH.md + scripts/email-intake-oauth.mjs
# PADOVA_EMAIL_INTAKE_CLIENT_ID=
# PADOVA_EMAIL_INTAKE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Prefer one refresh token per mailbox (run OAuth helper twice):
# PADOVA_EMAIL_INTAKE_REFRESH_TOKEN_SHMUEL=
# PADOVA_EMAIL_INTAKE_REFRESH_TOKEN_MINDY=
# Optional shared fallback if only one mailbox granted:
# PADOVA_EMAIL_INTAKE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# PADOVA_EMAIL_INTAKE_ACTOR_ID=active-staff-uuid
# PADOVA_EMAIL_INTAKE_CRON_SECRET=long-random-for-POST-/api/booking-intake/email/poll
# Poll: POST /api/booking-intake/email/poll (staff session or Bearer cron secret)
# npm run intake:email-oauth -- --mailbox=Shmuel@padovatravel.com

# Instinct WhatsApp agent (Stage 1) — draft-only HTTP intake. Never posts money.
# Give Instinct the QA URL + token as a custom HTTP action / capability.
# PADOVA_INSTINCT_TOKEN=long-random-secret
# PADOVA_INSTINCT_ACTOR_ID=active-staff-uuid
# Endpoint: POST https://qa.padovatravel.com/api/booking-intake/instinct
# Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>  (or x-padova-instinct: <token>)
# Body JSON: { "text": "reservation paste or Field:Value lines", "chat_name": "optional" }
# See docs/INSTINCT_INTEGRATION.md

# WhatsApp PC read-only bridge (Phase 4) — never Meta Cloud API send.
# Server needs the token. Owner-PC script also needs URL + actor id (can live in .env.local).
# PADOVA_WHATSAPP_BRIDGE_TOKEN=
# PADOVA_WHATSAPP_BRIDGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/booking-intake/whatsapp
# PADOVA_WHATSAPP_ACTOR_ID=active-staff-uuid
# PADOVA_WHATSAPP_INBOX_DIR=.data/whatsapp-inbox
# PADOVA_WHATSAPP_AUTH_DIR=.data/whatsapp-web-auth
# PADOVA_WHATSAPP_UI_PORT=3927
# PADOVA_WHATSAPP_UI_HOST=127.0.0.1
# Or: .data/whatsapp-helper-config.json (see scripts/whatsapp-pc-helper/config.example.json)
# Owner double-click: scripts/whatsapp-pc-helper/Start-Padova-WhatsApp.command|.bat
# npm run intake:whatsapp-helper       — auto-opens browser QR page on this PC
# npm run intake:whatsapp-bridge -- check|once|watch|stdin  — folder/stdin helper
# Unofficial linked session: residual ToS/ban risk; PC must stay online; never auto-sends.
# Not a public internet login URL — session stays on the Owner PC.

